<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 4 Convergence analysis ‣ MeCeFO: Enhancing LLM Training Robustness via Fault-Tolerant Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First, we specify the update rules of MeCeFO with momentum SGD as follows:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{m}^{(t)}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒎</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{m}^{(t)}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta_{1}\bm{m}^{(t-1)}+(1-\beta_{1})\overline{\bm{g}}^{(t)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒎</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒈</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta_{1}\bm{m}^{(t-1)}+(1-\beta_{1})\overline{\bm{g}}^{(t)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{w}^{(t+1)}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{w}^{(t+1)}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{w}^{(t)}-\eta\bm{m}^{(t)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒎</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{w}^{(t)}-\eta\bm{m}^{(t)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\bm{g}}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒈</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\bm{g}}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> is MeCeFO’s averaged weight gradient, <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{m}^{(-1)}=\bm{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒎</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{m}^{(-1)}=\bm{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> is the momentum parameter, <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is the learning rate.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we present several key lemmas.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Descent lemma)<span id="Thmlemma1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Lower-boundedness and 𝐿-smoothness). ‣ 4 Convergence analysis ‣ MeCeFO: Enhancing LLM Training Robustness via Fault-Tolerant Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\bm{w}^{(t+1)})\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\bm{w}^{(t+1)})\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\bm{w}^{(t)})-\left(\frac{1}{2\eta}-\frac{L}{2}\right)\|\bm{w}^{(t+1)}-\bm{w}^{(t)}\|_{2}^{2}+\frac{\eta}{2}\|\nabla f(\bm{w}^{(t)})-\bm{m}^{(t)}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝒎</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\bm{w}^{(t)})-\left(\frac{1}{2\eta}-\frac{L}{2}\right)\|\bm{w}^{(t+1)}-\bm{w}^{(t)}\|_{2}^{2}+\frac{\eta}{2}\|\nabla f(\bm{w}^{(t)})-\bm{m}^{(t)}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{\eta}{2}\|\nabla f(\bm{w}^{(t)})\|_{2}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{\eta}{2}\|\nabla f(\bm{w}^{(t)})\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Descent lemma). ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ MeCeFO: Enhancing LLM Training Robustness via Fault-Tolerant Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothness of <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> (Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Lower-boundedness and 𝐿-smoothness). ‣ 4 Convergence analysis ‣ MeCeFO: Enhancing LLM Training Robustness via Fault-Tolerant Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\bm{w}^{(t+1)})\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\bm{w}^{(t+1)})\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\bm{w}^{(t)})+\langle\nabla f(\bm{w}^{(t)}),\bm{w}^{(t+1)}-\bm{w}^{(t)}\rangle+\frac{L}{2}\|\bm{w}^{(t+1)}-\bm{w}^{(t)}\|_{2}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\bm{w}^{(t)})+\langle\nabla f(\bm{w}^{(t)}),\bm{w}^{(t+1)}-\bm{w}^{(t)}\rangle+\frac{L}{2}\|\bm{w}^{(t+1)}-\bm{w}^{(t)}\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">For the inner product, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle\nabla f(\bm{w}^{(t)}),\bm{w}^{(t+1)}-\bm{w}^{(t)}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle\nabla f(\bm{w}^{(t)}),\bm{w}^{(t+1)}-\bm{w}^{(t)}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\langle\frac{\bm{m}^{(t)}}{2},\bm{w}^{(t+1)}-\bm{w}^{(t)}\right\rangle+\left\langle\nabla f(\bm{w}^{(t)})-\frac{\bm{m}^{(t)}}{2},\bm{w}^{(t+1)}-\bm{w}^{(t)}\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>𝒎</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>𝒎</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\langle\frac{\bm{m}^{(t)}}{2},\bm{w}^{(t+1)}-\bm{w}^{(t)}\right\rangle+\left\langle\nabla f(\bm{w}^{(t)})-\frac{\bm{m}^{(t)}}{2},\bm{w}^{(t+1)}-\bm{w}^{(t)}\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{1}{2\eta}\|\bm{w}^{(t+1)}-\bm{w}^{(t)}\|_{2}^{2}+\frac{\eta}{2}\|\nabla f(\bm{w}^{(t)})-\bm{m}^{(t)}\|_{2}^{2}-\frac{\eta}{2}\|\nabla f(\bm{w}^{(t)})\|_{2}^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝒎</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{1}{2\eta}\|\bm{w}^{(t+1)}-\bm{w}^{(t)}\|_{2}^{2}+\frac{\eta}{2}\|\nabla f(\bm{w}^{(t)})-\bm{m}^{(t)}\|_{2}^{2}-\frac{\eta}{2}\|\nabla f(\bm{w}^{(t)})\|_{2}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the last equality uses <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{w}^{(t+1)}-\bm{w}^{(t)}=-\eta\bm{m}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒎</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{w}^{(t+1)}-\bm{w}^{(t)}=-\eta\bm{m}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying (<a href="#A1.E5" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ MeCeFO: Enhancing LLM Training Robustness via Fault-Tolerant Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) to (<a href="#A1.E4" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ MeCeFO: Enhancing LLM Training Robustness via Fault-Tolerant Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) yields (<a href="#A1.E3" title="In Lemma 1 (Descent lemma). ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ MeCeFO: Enhancing LLM Training Robustness via Fault-Tolerant Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Momentum-gradient gap)<span id="Thmlemma2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Lower-boundedness and 𝐿-smoothness). ‣ 4 Convergence analysis ‣ MeCeFO: Enhancing LLM Training Robustness via Fault-Tolerant Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Stochastic gradient). ‣ 4 Convergence analysis ‣ MeCeFO: Enhancing LLM Training Robustness via Fault-Tolerant Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3 (Gradient error). ‣ 4 Convergence analysis ‣ MeCeFO: Enhancing LLM Training Robustness via Fault-Tolerant Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{T+1}\sum_{t=0}^{T}\mathbb{E}[\|\bm{m}^{(t)}-\nabla f(\bm{w}^{(t)})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>𝒎</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{T+1}\sum_{t=0}^{T}\mathbb{E}[\|\bm{m}^{(t)}-\nabla f(\bm{w}^{(t)})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{2\Delta_{1}}{(1-\beta_{1})(T+1)}+\frac{4L^{2}}{\delta(1-\beta_{1})^{2}}\cdot\frac{1}{T+1}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}[\|\bm{w}^{(t)}-\bm{w}^{(t-1)}\|_{2}^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{2\Delta_{1}}{(1-\beta_{1})(T+1)}+\frac{4L^{2}}{\delta(1-\beta_{1})^{2}}\cdot\frac{1}{T+1}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}[\|\bm{w}^{(t)}-\bm{w}^{(t-1)}\|_{2}^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
